{
 "rule": "The Vision-to-contract mapping takes VNFaceObservation angles (radians) to contract Euler degrees in the display-upright head frame. `orientation` is the EXIF orientation handed to VNImageRequestHandler, i.e. the stored stream's orientation, so Vision measured the upright (un-mirrored) image; the mapping is therefore a unit conversion plus range normalisation for every orientation.",
 "contract": "spec/frames-and-units.md \u00a73",
 "assumed_vision_convention": "Vision angles are right-hand rotations about the axes of its upright image frame (x right, y up, z out of the image toward the viewer), composed as Ry(yaw) . Rx(pitch) . Rz(roll), with the face looking at the camera = 0. Authored from Apple's documented image-space convention (lower-left origin, y up); NOT yet verified on a device (`verified_on_device: false`). A confirmed sign flip is a change to these vectors.",
 "algorithm": "contract = euler(Ry.Rx.Rz(vision)) (degrees; yaw, roll wrapped to [-180,180)). The stored pose of the same head is orientation-dependent: see upright_euler.json.",
